## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical Azure-native data path design, governance, and cost controls for a multi-tenant SaaS.

## Key Concepts
- REST ingestion with serverless compute (Azure Functions)
- ADLS Gen2 with tenant-prefixed folders for per-tenant isolation
- Data Factory for hourly pipeline orchestration
- Purview for data governance and lineage tracking
- Synapse for analytics and Azure ML for anomaly detection
- Paired region DR and budget-based controls for data residency

## Code Example
```javascript
// Azure Function to trigger Data Factory pipeline on schedule
export default async function (context, req) {
    const pipelineRunner = await context.executionContext.getBindingData();

    const response = await fetch('https://management.azure.com/subscriptions/{subscription-id}/resourceGroups/{rg}/providers/Microsoft.DataFactory/factories/{df}/pipelines/WeatherIngestionPipeline/createRun?api-version=2018-06-01', {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: {
            'Authorization': `Bearer ${process.env.ARM_TOKEN}`,
            'Content-Type': 'application/json'
        }
    });

    context.log('Pipeline triggered:', response.status);
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end Azure-native, multi-tenant data platform design under regulatory constraints with real-time processing, governance, security, disaster recovery, and cost discipline.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant isolation and per-tenant policy enforcement
- EU data residency with bring-your-own-key (BYOK) encryption
- Real-time event processing using Durable Functions
- Data governance with Purview and token-based sharing mechanisms
- Disaster recovery to paired region with automated failover strategies
- Cost optimization through serverless analytics, auto-scaling, and resource quotas

## Code Example
```javascript
// Durable Function snippet: policy check and redaction (pseudo-code)
module.exports = async function (context, req) {
  const tenantId = req.headers['x-tenant-id'];
  const eventData = req.body;

  // Per-tenant policy validation
  const policy = await getTenantPolicy(tenantId);
  if (!validateEvent(eventData, policy)) {
    context.res = { status: 403, body: 'Policy violation' };
    return;
  }

  // PII redaction
  const redactedData = redactPII(eventData, policy.piiRules);

  // Store to ADLS and trigger downstream processing
  await storeToADLS(tenantId, redactedData);
  await triggerSynapseProcessing(tenantId, redactedData);
};
```

